hifted (1y 1.43 vs 5y 0.87), so read it loosely.","About $13.0M trades a day, enough to build a position.","In past sell-offs it fell 81% in the 2020 crash, 43% in the 2022 bear market and 78% in 2008."],"val":["The stock trades 56% below its DCF fair value of $66.89, a meaningful margin of safety.","The fair-value models disagree (dispersion 18%), and the Monte Carlo range runs $54.79 to $83.68 (P10-P90), so treat the estimate as noisy.","On multiples it looks cheap against Consumer Cyclical peers: P/E 7.3 vs 18.8, EV/EBITDA 6.5 vs 10.7 and P/FCF 9.2 vs 16.7 (sector median).","Against its own history it is cheap: the EBIT multiple sits 25% below its 10-year median.","Earnings yields are attractive: an FCF yield of 10.9% (above the risk-free rate) and an EBIT/EV of 14.8% (vs the 8% bar).","The 3 covering analysts target $45.00 on average, 53% above the price, well away from the model's fair value."],"prof":["ROIC of 65% clears the cost of capital of 9.3% by 56pp, the mark of a value creator; returns have swung a lot from year to year (CV 2.70).","It runs a 53% gross margin and converts 7% of revenue into free cash flow.","Earnings quality looks solid: cash conversion of 1.25x.","ROE of 34% comes mostly from margins and asset turnover rather than leverage (2.2x equity multiplier).","Operating margin is running 7pp above its own historical average, a peak-margin risk if conditions normalise.","It spends 0.6% of revenue on stock compensation."],"hlth":["The balance sheet carries net cash of $26.8M (7% of market cap).","No distress or manipulation flags (Altman Z 3.9, in the safe zone)."],"growth":["Revenue has compounded at 4.2% over 3 years, 5.2% over 5 years and 3.8% over 10 years, and it has been lumpy (year-to-year swings of 19%).","At current returns, reinvesting 25% of profits supports about 16.3% a year of fundamental growth, enough to sustain growth.","Free cash flow has compounded 14.6% a year over five years.","Margins are expanding (+1.1% trend).","Forward indicators: deferred revenue down 20%.","Capex runs 1.7x depreciation (4.8% of sales), so it is building capacity for future growth."],"own":["Insiders own 5.6%, meaningful skin in the game, and reported institutional holdings exceed 100% of shares (a sign of heavy share lending).","It returns 10.8% a year to shareholders (7.7% in buybacks and 3.1% in dividends).","The share count has shrunk 5.2% a year over five years, steadily raising each holder's stake.","Short interest is elevated at 25.7% of the float, 7.4 days to cover."],"people":["With about 1,200 employees, each generates about $442K of revenue, 1.2x the Consumer Cyclical median.","That works out to $33K of free cash flow per employee.","CEO pay is $850K (2x revenue per employee), and compensation governance scores well (3/10, lower is better).","Stock compensation averages $2K per employee."]},"profile":{"v":"INVEST","conv":85,"head":"Invest: trades 56% below fair value of $66.89; ROIC 65.1% vs WACC 9.3%.","pros":["Composite 71, above the 57 line (gates 20/25)","Trades 56% below fair value of $66.89","ROIC 65.1% vs WACC 9.3%","Net cash of $26.8M","Altman Z in the safe zone"],"cons":["12-1 month momentum -48%"],"flags":[],"need":[],"buy_below":56.86,"vc":{"base":66.89,"base_src":"dcf","bear":54.79,"bull":83.68,"alt_median":48.48,"n_alt":3,"gap":0.3798,"dispersion":0.1824,"level":"MEDIUM","why":[]},"med":{"pe":18.8184,"ev_ebitda":10.707,"pfcf":16.6971,"pb":2.3,"roic":0.1268,"gross_margin":0.346,"fcf_margin":0.0621,"div_yield":0.0232}},"mc_quantiles":[46.31,52.13,54.79,57.01,58.73,60.31,61.53,62.91,64.59,65.95,67.18,68.68,70.39,71.79,73.08,74.98,77.14,79.87,83.68,89.04,102.62],"mc_drivers":{"growth":0.447,"discount_rate":0.417,"terminal_growth":0.025,"exit_multiple":0.111},"ticker":"BBW","date":"2026-11-13"}